Unfortunately, the PR doesn't fix the bug. If you try to run the tests, you may find out that it just makes the findKey utility useless and breaks other related code. The problem is inside [mergeConfig](https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/cda671af81ca87a00c6bf5a07bffcb07468756d3/lib/core/mergeConfig.js#L17) util due to function params overlapping. Every merge handler [is called](https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/cda671af81ca87a00c6bf5a07bffcb07468756d3/lib/core/mergeConfig.js#L101) with the property name as the third argument, but [mergeDeepProperties](https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/cda671af81ca87a00c6bf5a07bffcb07468756d3/lib/core/mergeConfig.js#L34) and [getMergedValue](https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/cda671af81ca87a00c6bf5a07bffcb07468756d3/lib/core/mergeConfig.js#L22) expect `caseless` argument instead so this causes the bug.
So we can fix this by inserting the missing prop argument into the functions definition and fixing their calls
```js
function getMergedValue(target, source, prop, caseless) {...}
function mergeDeepProperties(a, b, prop, caseless) {
// fix call
headers: (a, b, prop) => mergeDeepProperties(headersToObject(a), headersToObject(b), prop, true)
```

